PLAN-165 P2 — register `night_mode_toggled` (round-2 revision, NM-05 / NM-08)

ATOMICITY REQUIREMENT (why this patch and the script emit are ONE ceremony
deliverable): emitting an unregistered action makes reality-ledger detector 6
(`test_reality_ledger.py::test_detector_6_no_phantoms_at_head`) and the
audit-registry coverage checker
(`test_check_audit_registry_coverage.py::TestRealRepoSmoke::test_real_repo_exit_0`)
go red — and those guards are CORRECT: an emit call site with no registration
is exactly the phantom-action class they exist to catch. So the emit in
`.claude/scripts/night-mode.py` and its registration here must land in the
SAME ceremony, atomically — never a commit at whose HEAD the emit exists
unregistered. The round-2 fix pass therefore REMOVED the pre-registration
emit from the staged `night-mode.py` (it was a breadcrumb-only dead call and
it redded both guards), and this ceremony re-adds it.

Mechanics: `night-mode.py` does not exist at canonical HEAD (W1 is blocked on
this very ceremony), so the script-side emit CANNOT be expressed as a diff
hunk in this patch — a hunk against a nonexistent file fails
`git apply --check`, and the staged script is still being revised by the
round-2 fix pass, so no context lines can be guaranteed. The emit is instead
specified as a mandatory, precisely-located instruction block + self-contained
snippet in README.md §"P2 emit re-insertion (MANDATORY — same ceremony)".
The ceremony executor MUST complete that block: registration lands with this
patch; the emit lands in the same ceremony's W1-land commit (the first commit
that puts `night-mode.py` at HEAD), with-or-after registration, never before.
Per NM-05 the emit fires on EVERY terminating path of `on`/`off` with the
matching result enum member (applied / noop / refused / failed), inside a
try/except no-op envelope, with ONLY the fields mode, previous_mode, result,
hostname_hash.

